There are some edge cases that need to be fixed:

1. Intermediate and Advanced are missing the rear hook (punch #4). It has been missing from the beginning. It should be included the same way the lead hook (#3) is included.

2. The slip mechanics are wrong, and possibly some other defensive movements too, but I haven’t checked those yet.

* After a slip right, the app called a lead hook (#3). Biomechanically that makes no sense because the body position after slipping right naturally loads the rear side. After a slip right, the next punch should be a rear-hand punch (#2 cross, #4 rear hook, #6 rear uppercut, etc.).
* Same issue with slip left. It then called a cross (#2), but the body position after slipping left naturally loads the lead side. After a slip left, the next punch should be a lead-hand punch (#1 jab, #3 lead hook, #5 lead uppercut, etc.).

3. One of the Intermediate rounds used “pivot left” repeatedly for almost the entire 3 minutes. The system should rotate between pivots and all other footwork options more evenly. Repetition is the worst enemy here — combos and movement need to feel varied and dynamic.
